{"text": "SWERSITy.\n\nSs Centre for Anatomy and Human Identification\n\nUniversity of Dundee\nyy L Dundee DDI 5EH\nScotland, UK.\n\u00b0\n\nDUNDEE \u2018Tel. 044 1382 38576\n\n\u2018The Honourable Mr. A.G. Van der Steur\nMinister of Security and Justice\nMinistry of Security and Justice\nP.O. Box 20301\n2500 EH The Hague\n\u2018The Netherlands|\n\nCe:\n- Drs. H.W.M. Schoof, National Coordinator for Security and Counterterrorism\n-Mr. , Head of the National Team Forensic Investigation\n= Mr! |, Operational Head of the National Team Forensic Investigation\n\n\u2018st May 2015\nDear Minister Van der Steur,\n\n\u2018The undersigned represent international colleagues and friends of Professor George Maat who wish to\nbring their views to your attention, In recent days there have been many regrettable media articles in.\nrelation to a lecture intended for medical students but which unfortunately resulted in public\nexposure to images and dialogue associated with the victims of the MHI7 airplane crash.\n\nGeorge Maat is a world leading authority and one of the most experienced forensic practitioners in\ndisaster victim identification. His expertise has been called upon, without incident, in response to\nmass fatality events which include Balkan War Crimes, $.A. Fireworks in Enschede, the South East\nAsian Tsunami and many airplanes crashes across the world. With his colleagues, he has worked\ntirelessly and to the best of his ability to bring comfort and closure to the families and friends of\nvictims whilst unreservedly supporting justice.\n\nHe is a highly regarded and frequently cited academic and his research has had great impact on\nforensic and medical education at a global scale. His outstanding leadership has been recognised by\nhis community on many occasions resulting in a long list of national and international awards.\nProfessor Maat is a consummate professional, a man of integrity and empathy and a role model for\naspiring young scientists and practitioners.\n\nIt is with great regret that the incident unfolded and escalated as it did and we are certain there was\nno malfeasance or mal intent intended. Knowing Professor Maat as we all do, and in light of his,\nheartfelt and genuine public apology, we are all ofthe firm belief that the situation was borne out of\n\n46",
